-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">been thinking a bit how does a skindancer reach Rituals 5? By acting as an assistant to a garou ritemaster? an intensive training course lasting YEARS given by a realized skindancer, or let an allready established skindancer perform the rite on his behalf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hedge Magic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T13:46:42-08:00","id":827758,"title":"","content":"or a good many Would be skindancers are screwed over by lack of Rituals struggling to learn it get caught shamed and beheaded in front of the sept...<br /> <br /> Many should have a lot of Numina too I think... Sam Haight I know his names almost an expletive... Mage spheres dont belong in the hands of Garou, but I think lots of numina makes sense maybe some &quot;Equipment background&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T14:16:29-08:00","id":827780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/827707-how-do-skindancers-achieve-rituals-5?p=827725#post827725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is how I normally handle it. It does go against the canon ritual, but it makes a lot more sense than having that many kinfolk with Rituals 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I'd handle it as well. It also supports the idea of community among the skin dancers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T14:23:20-08:00","id":827788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/827707-how-do-skindancers-achieve-rituals-5?p=827758#post827758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or a good many Would be skindancers are screwed over by lack of Rituals struggling to learn it get caught shamed and beheaded in front of the sept...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of the point. It takes a very special kind of Person to actually become a Skindancer. There are only a few people in the world with the dedication and knowledge to pursue things like these, making them some of the scariest folks around.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T21:32:16-08:00","id":827982,"title":"","content":"I have run a few games based around Skin Dancers. One thing to remember is that all of them are/were Kinfolk. Kinfolk that live among the Garou are no strangers of how to participate in common rite or how to behave with elders and leaders even if they don't often reap the benefits of the act itself. Ritual as a knowledge is not necessarily the ability to conjure magical effect but the ability to perform a series of actions according to a prescribed order.<br /> <br /> That said, in all of my games they are all have Sorcery. Ritual only arts though like Summoning/Binding/Warding or Enchantment. These seemed like the most appropriate given that they have had quite a bit of success with dealing with spirits despite having never been formally taught the Rites Garou use to achieve the same ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T21:35:11-08:00","id":827985,"title":"","content":"Banes and other nastiness teaching them, profane knowledge is easy to come by if you want it bad enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T21:58:14-08:00","id":827996,"title":"","content":"I never bought this requiring everyone to have level 5 in Rituals. I have it there are a Few Skin Dansers who perform it for others, or a Sorcery Ritual, which is more fitting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T19:47:35-08:00","id":828565,"title":"","content":"In my chronicle, Sam Haight was not the first Skin Dancer. It is an old tradition the Garou keep covering up. But there are old and rare books and lore out there that describe how to perform the Rite, and therefore how to train oneself into obtaining the requisite ranks in the Rituals ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T00:23:38-08:00","id":829606,"title":"","content":"I've used skinners sparingly over the years. However I did do a history on the rite at one point. I'm not entirely certain where that notebook is or even if it still exists but from memory: The rite of Sacred Rebirth was created during the days of the War of Rage not by the Garou but by the Bastet. The Bastet of India used this rite to inflame jealously among the kin of the Garou. As the Garou turned on the human kin the Bagheera and Khan struck the wolf kin and drove the Garou north. The war of Rage in India was turned sideways when someone among the Bastet kin was taught the rite. Both sides came to an accord a d the War stopped. Both sides destroyed any skin dancers left all copies were destroyed, except one hidden by the Bagheera that created the rite.<br /> I think this was going to be used in a chronicle of lost secrets I do remember I had a good bit more detail in the original.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}